  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 210,
    "dDurationMs": 5339,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The Universe. How big is it? Does it have\na center? Does it have an edge? Is it getting"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 5549,
    "dDurationMs": 2250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "bigger, and if so, why?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 7799,
    "dDurationMs": 4411,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, we know that there are two different\nmeanings for \"universe\" - first, the \"observable"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 12210,
    "dDurationMs": 4340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "universe\" is everything that we've been able\nto see, or observe, thus far. And second,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 16550,
    "dDurationMs": 4869,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"The Universe\" (or \"the whole universe\") means\neverything that exists or has existed, or"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 21419,
    "dDurationMs": 1041,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "will exist."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 22460,
    "dDurationMs": 4479,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "More specifically, the observable universe\nis the region of space visible to us from"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 26939,
    "dDurationMs": 5210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "earth. And since The Universe is only about\n13.8 billion years old and light takes time"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 32149,
    "dDurationMs": 3890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to travel through space, then regardless of\nwhat direction we look, we see light that's"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 36039,
    "dDurationMs": 5070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "been traveling (at most) 13.8 billion years.\nSo it's logical to think that the observable"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 41109,
    "dDurationMs": 7000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "universe must then be 2*13.77 = 27.5 billion\nlight years across - but it's not. That's"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 48160,
    "dDurationMs": 4449,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because over time, space has been expanding,\nso the distant objects that gave off that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 52609,
    "dDurationMs": 5741,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "light 13.8 billion years ago have since moved\neven farther away from us. Today, those distant"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 58350,
    "dDurationMs": 4820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "objects are a bit more than 46 billion light\nyears away. Multiply times two and you get"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 63170,
    "dDurationMs": 4430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "93 billion light years: the diameter of the\nobservable universe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 67600,
    "dDurationMs": 3699,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To give you a sense of scale, the size of\nthe earth within the observable universe is"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 71299,
    "dDurationMs": 4341,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "roughly equivalent to the size of a virus\nwithin the solar system - although that doesn't"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 75640,
    "dDurationMs": 3890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "help much because we can't really appreciate\nthe incomprehensible smallness of a virus"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 79530,
    "dDurationMs": 3060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "nor the bewildering bigness of the solar system,\neither."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 82590,
    "dDurationMs": 4650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So let's just say that the observable universe\nis stupendously big. But The Whole Universe,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 87240,
    "dDurationMs": 6210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as far as we can tell, is a lot bigger - space\nis most likely infinite! Or at least it doesn't"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 93450,
    "dDurationMs": 4029,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "have an edge, though the difference between\nthose is another story unto itself."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 97479,
    "dDurationMs": 4691,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, what about the center of the universe?\nWell the observable universe has a center"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 102170,
    "dDurationMs": 4470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Us! We're at the center of the observable\nuniverse because the observable universe is"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 106640,
    "dDurationMs": 4409,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "just the region of space visible from earth,\nand kind of like how the view from a very"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 111049,
    "dDurationMs": 4460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "tall tower is a circle centered on the tower,\nthe piece of space we can see from here is"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 115509,
    "dDurationMs": 4860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "naturally centered here. In fact, if you want\nto be more precise, EACH ONE OF US is the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 120369,
    "dDurationMs": 2430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "center of our OWN observable universe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 122799,
    "dDurationMs": 3380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But that doesn't mean we're at the center\nof The Whole Universe, just like the tower"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 126179,
    "dDurationMs": 3791,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "isn't the center of the world - it's the center\nof the piece of the world that it can see"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 129970,
    "dDurationMs": 4340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- up to the horizon. But just because you\ncan't see beyond the horizon doesn't mean"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 134310,
    "dDurationMs": 1550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there's nothing there."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 135860,
    "dDurationMs": 3690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And so it is with the observable universe.\nLooking up at the sky, we see light light"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 139550,
    "dDurationMs": 4760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that's at most 13.8 billion years old and\ncoming from stuff that's now 46 billion light"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 144310,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "years away. Anything farther is \"beyond the\nhorizon\". But each second, we see new, even"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 149910,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "older light coming from slightly farther away\n(one light-second farther, to be precise),"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 154910,
    "dDurationMs": 4060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and so our view of the cosmos is literally\ngetting bigger all the time - all we have"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 158970,
    "dDurationMs": 4470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to do is wait and watch as the universe ages\nand light from more distant places has the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 163440,
    "dDurationMs": 1500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "time to get to us."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 164940,
    "dDurationMs": 5060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So here we are, sitting at the center of our\nobservable piece of the Whole Universe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 170000,
    "dDurationMs": 4870,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "How big is the universe? Well, the observable\nuniverse is currently 93 billion light years"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 174870,
    "dDurationMs": 6640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "across. The Whole Universe is probably infinite.\nDoes the universe have an edge? The observable"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 181510,
    "dDurationMs": 4470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "does (it's 46 billion light years away in\nany direction), and The Whole Universe has"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 185980,
    "dDurationMs": 4910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a temporal edge (or what we call a beginning)\nbut almost certainly not a spatial one."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 190890,
    "dDurationMs": 4620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Does the universe have a center? Again, the\nobservable universe does: YOU! The Universe"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 195510,
    "dDurationMs": 4910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as a whole? Almost certainly not.\nAnd is the universe getting bigger? Yes - space"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 200420,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is expanding, which makes both the observable\nuniverse and the whole universe bigger - plus,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 204980,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "over time, we see older and older light coming\nfrom farther and farther away, so our observable"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 209940,
    "dDurationMs": 1990,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "universe gets bigger that way, too."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 211930,
    "dDurationMs": 4910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And that, in a nutshell, is our view from\nthe tower. You are the center of the universe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 216840,
    "dDurationMs": 7000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And so am I. And so is everyone else. And\nso is no one."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 223859,
    "dDurationMs": 3671,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "0"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 227530,
    "dDurationMs": 3099,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this episode a minute physics is\nsupported by Audible dot com"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 230629,
    "dDurationMs": 3241,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the leading provider are you books\nacross all types a literature including"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 233870,
    "dDurationMs": 2110,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "fiction and non-fiction and periodicals"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 235980,
    "dDurationMs": 3349,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to learn more about why we think the\nuniverse has the size and shape that we"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 239329,
    "dDurationMs": 910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "think it does"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 240239,
    "dDurationMs": 3881,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "check out how the universe got its spots\nby Jan 11 you could download this"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 244120,
    "dDurationMs": 1670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "audiobook for another of your choice"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 245790,
    "dDurationMs": 3619,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for free artful dot com slash minute\nphysics again thanks talkable"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 249409,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "making it possible for me to keep\nproducing minute physics and for giving"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 251969,
    "dDurationMs": 2890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you a free audiobook an audible dot com\nslash minute physics"
    } ]
  } ]
}
